/target

.env
# Any sibling of it too: a `.env.bak` from an edit, a `.env.local`,
# a `.env.old`. The file holds node secrets and a funded
# deployer key, and a backup of it is exactly as sensitive as the
# original while being one `git add -A` from a commit.
.env.*

**/target/
**/test_snapshots/
# Contract lockfiles are TRACKED: the wasm must rebuild byte for byte, and
# rust-toolchain.toml alone does not pin dependencies. With them, a
# deployed mint or roster can be rebuilt exactly from its commit.

# System-test run logs. Every run records the addresses it funded and used,
# which is exactly the link between this code and a person that docs/TESTNET.md
# deliberately keeps out of the repository. The logs are run artifacts - read
# them locally, do not publish them.
docs/systest-runs/

# Documentation site build output and dependencies
docs/node_modules/
docs/.vitepress/dist/
docs/.vitepress/cache/

# Release packages (packaging/)
/dist/
